{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 84","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(credit_to_official_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (credit to official solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_84&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> for which the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2291d0d977c0f0543151cf9f6115e2deba881b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+bx+2008b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> can be factored over the integers. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11ceba9d7455309f60178fe82bb6e81e6c01fa83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_84&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28credit_to_official_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(credit_to_official_solution)\">Solution 1 (credit to official solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_84&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (credit to official solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the roots of the quadratic be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.  By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055368d683fe39dbd7822e1a70615a9f2b0ec07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s = -b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c889d12451d321614e219737373586e45b71a141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs$\" width=\"16\" height=\"8\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09f433ff1e9f19148f008e12cd9e54c386f85dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008b$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe know that one of the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is 0 because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has integer roots.  However, adding or removing 0 does not affect the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, so we can divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa30e2beb1820f6b39f6251023709c8165cefc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />.  Doing so results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/5405bdbb0ee1d0882942e3190a9f56a14c7017ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{rs}{r+s} &amp;= -2008 \\\\ rs &amp;= -2008r - 2008s \\\\ rs + 2008r + 2008s &amp;= 0 \\\\ (r+2008)(s+2008) &amp;= 2008^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"310\" height=\"111\" />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00de4ae01e5dd9c4a1ded6ff2ad82408a5a64e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a| \\le 2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4ee918bf442fcbcdcae0eec2ae37e1b522b8957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008^2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/6/146fea2bbbece8a18bfa8734e972940ac3857d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+2008 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1efb64fa31de6fa5d02863cad9a409ae656cd185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+2008 = \\tfrac{2008^2}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"126\" height=\"24\" />.  Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d22822dee85550ba4a8b670d7c31ba999c1f3287.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-r-s = b = -a - \\tfrac{2008^2}{a} + 4016.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"24\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be positive or negative, the positive values cancel with the negative values.  The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4ee918bf442fcbcdcae0eec2ae37e1b522b8957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008^2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb4c79490ebb3ec86bd3ea41e4440b02aa42628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6 \\cdot 251^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6a020383c3b956130e8be5a46eb7b9fed6c30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21+2}{2} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" /> positive factors that are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc1744a459ad135efd3fd45fca7285cae133717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so the absolute value of the sum of all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b6f73929432b668ea2e62b970c27bd297219f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4016 \\cdot 22 = \\boxed{88352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_84&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The discriminant of the function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f8f14112022e003e9a3e4786d74058c8f99514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - 8032b$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />.  Since all roots are integers and leading term is 1, the discriminant must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/688bdb3e162dae282e816fe540e8cad67c5a56c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} b^2 - 8032b =&amp; n^2 \\\\ (b-4016)^2 - n^2 &amp;= 4016^2 \\\\ (b-4016+n)(b-4016-n) &amp;= 4016^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"297\" height=\"75\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d8212f8d769a24be01b7d764d3e026bb0bfe95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4016^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090f836ad06228c81403bc3fb8c7f5317986ab3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} b - 4016 + n &amp;= x \\\\ b - 4016 - n &amp;= \\frac{4016^2}{x} \\\\ b &amp;= 4016 + \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{4016^2}{2x} \\end{align*}\" width=\"264\" height=\"109\" />\nNote that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edbc45e51273ae9d83a59b0be7be6d43429f1636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{4016^2}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"35\" height=\"24\" /> is even, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> can not be an integer.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be even.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/1536f9b73d2c7e2b69c3bb9149ffa378ce557771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/4852ed905d1e7bdcfb755afea7583417c1c43801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 4016 + y + \\frac{2008^2}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"168\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f640448384790bd22c28e3c2c4b93141856272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_0 = \\frac{2008^2}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"86\" height=\"42\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db1f200e8f7fe71429956e2df3a853934dc214bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + \\tfrac{2008^2}{y} = y_0 + \\tfrac{2008^2}{y_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" />.  Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can be positive or negative, the positive values cancel with the negative values.  So <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/12097de43d6fcd4914aa0fb29f7ccab864d7f24f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y| \\le 2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4ee918bf442fcbcdcae0eec2ae37e1b522b8957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008^2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb4c79490ebb3ec86bd3ea41e4440b02aa42628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6 \\cdot 251^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6a020383c3b956130e8be5a46eb7b9fed6c30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21+2}{2} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" /> positive factors that are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc1744a459ad135efd3fd45fca7285cae133717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so the absolute value of the sum of all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b6f73929432b668ea2e62b970c27bd297219f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4016 \\cdot 22 = \\boxed{88352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_84&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_83\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 83\">Problem 83</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_85\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 85\">Problem 85</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1